从布鲁克林到布法罗，从锡拉丘兹到南港，他们已经准备好在世界上留下自己的印记。

124
00:12:04,880 --> 00:12:06,880
But I hear their anxieties as well.
但我也听到了他们的焦虑。

125
00:12:07,464 --> 00:12:18,240
The college graduate who worked hard for that degree only to worry that they AI could take the job that they spent years preparing
那些为这个学位而努力学习的大学毕业生却担心他们的人工智能会取代他们花了数年时间准备的工作

126
00:12:18,240 --> 00:12:25,660
For the young couple wondering if they'll be able to afford a new baby or grow up in the neighborhood where they grew up As well.
对于年轻夫妇来说，他们想知道他们是否能够负担得起新生儿或在他们长大的社区长大也是如此。

127
00:12:27,040 --> 00:12:32,595
As a mom and grandma, I know how much dreams matter.
作为妈妈和奶奶，我知道梦想有多么重要。

128
00:12:32,595 --> 00:12:34,606
But don't give up on them.
但不要放弃他们。

129
00:12:34,606 --> 00:12:43,030
Don't give up on New York because I believe our best days are ahead.
不要放弃纽约，因为我相信我们最好的日子就在前方。

130
00:12:43,040 --> 00:12:46,230
And I said this my first day as governor.
这是我担任州长的第一天说的。

131
00:12:46,290 --> 00:12:48,090
I'm not here to make history.
我来这里不是为了创造历史。

132
00:12:48,790 --> 00:12:50,630
I'm here to make a difference.
我来这里是为了做出改变。

133
00:12:51,750 --> 00:12:58,750
And when the story of my time in office is written, I don't want it to be about me.
当我写下我任职期间的故事时，我不希望它是关于我的。

134
00:12:59,710 --> 00:13:01,310
I want it to be about us.
我希望它是关于我们的。

135
00:13:02,270 --> 00:13:08,330
Rhonda, the lives we changed together, the families be lifted up and the doors be opened up for generations.
朗达，我们共同改变了生活，家庭得到提升，几代人的大门也被打开。

136
00:13:09,030 --> 00:13:09,850
We'll never know.
我们永远不会知道。

137
00:13:11,330 --> 00:13:15,072
Now, I see a lot of fun out there, a lot of festivities,
现在，我看到那里有很多乐趣，有很多庆祝活动，

138
00:13:15,530 --> 00:13:16,250
A lot of friendship.
很多友谊。

139
00:13:17,550 --> 00:13:20,390
Tomorrow, this room will be empty.
明天这个房间就空了。

140
00:13:22,160 --> 00:13:23,490
The victory party will be over.
胜利派对即将结束。

141
00:13:24,690 --> 00:13:28,410
And all across New York, families will get their kids ready for school,
纽约各地的家庭都会为孩子上学做好准备，

142
00:13:29,050 --> 00:13:32,110
Head off to work, and get on with their lives.
去工作，继续他们的生活。

143
00:13:32,890 --> 00:13:40,896
As for me, I too will get up and get right back to work because that's the promise I made when I became your Governor.
至于我，我也会起床并立即回去工作，因为这是我成为你时所做的承诺州长。

144
00:13:41,430 --> 00:13:44,090
And that's the promise I'll keep for the next four years.
这就是我在接下来的四年里将信守的承诺。

145
00:13:44,090 --> 00:13:48,465
That your family and your future are my fight.
你的家庭和你的未来是我的战斗。

146
00:13:48,465 --> 00:13:51,947
Together, let's keep lifting up.
让我们一起继续奋发向上。

147
00:13:51,947 --> 00:13:55,110
Upward and never.
向上且永不。

148
00:13:55,120 --> 00:13:57,309
God bless every single one of you.
愿上帝保佑你们每一个人。

149
00:13:57,309 --> 00:14:00,749
God bless the people of the great state of New York.
上帝保佑伟大的纽约州的人民。

150
00:14:00,749 --> 00:14:02,000
And God bless America.
上帝保佑美国。
